      "id": "c2",
      "kind": "choice",
      "prompt": "R is a rotation with trace -1 (angle pi). Which procedure gives its rotation axis?",
      "options": [
        "Compute vee(R - R^T) / (2 sin theta), which is well defined because R is symmetric there",
        "Take omega_i = sqrt((r_ii + 1)/2) for i=1,2,3 with all signs positive, which is exact at angle pi",
        "Normalise a nonzero column of R + I, which equals 2 w w^T, accepting that the sign of the axis is ambiguous",
        "Take the eigenvector of R with eigenvalue -1, which is the axis because the angle is pi"
      ],
      "answer": "2",
      "dimension": "C",
      "critical": false,
      "explanation": "At angle pi, R = 2ww^T - I, so R + I = 2ww^T and each nonzero column is proportional to w. The first option divides by sin(pi)=0 (and R-R^T=0); the second loses the relative signs fixed by r_ij = 2 w_i w_j; the eigenvalue -1 eigenspace is the plane perpendicular to the axis, not the axis."
    },
